# Optional. Leave this file alone unless the app cannot reach your API.
#
# Some endpoints simply cannot be called from a browser: they send no
# `Access-Control-Allow-Origin`, or their preflight answers
# `Access-Control-Allow-Headers: *` without naming `Authorization` — which the
# Fetch standard says does not count. Either way the request is blocked before
# it leaves the browser and no client-side setting can change that. A telling
# symptom is that `curl` reaches the same endpoint perfectly, because `curl`
# sends no preflight.
#
# Setting VITE_API_PROXY makes `npm run dev` serve that API from its own origin, so
# there is no cross-origin request left to block. It works with any provider —
# a local gateway, a self-hosted server, a remote API — and nothing outside
# this file knows which one you use.
#
#   1. cp .env.example .env.local
#   2. put your API's root below (no trailing /v1 — the app appends it)
#   3. npm run dev, then press «استفاده از proxy همین سرور» on the connect screen
#
# Examples:
#   VITE_API_PROXY=http://127.0.0.1:8080
#   VITE_API_PROXY=https://api.example.com
#
# Prefer 127.0.0.1 over localhost for a service on this machine: `localhost`
# resolves to ::1 first, and a service bound only to IPv4 is unreachable there.

VITE_API_PROXY=
